WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.050
The rehabilitation of the DC Extended Universe
continues with ﻿﻿Birds of Prey (And the

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.470
Fantabulous Emancipation of One Harley Quinn)﻿.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.510
The movie has screened for critics, and early
viewers are taking to social media to heap

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.620
praise on the Margot Robbie-led film.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.480
This is what they're saying.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.590
Joining Harley in her quest to bring the pain
to Ewan McGregor's Black Mask are a pair of

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:27.050
kickass antiheroes, a Gotham City cop, and
one scrappy kid.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.930
Jurnee Smollett-Bell portrays Black Canary,
while Mary Elizabeth Winstead holds down the

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:37.980
role of Huntress; they are flanked by Rosie
Perez's Detective Renee Montoya and Cassandra

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:44.239
Cain - a youngster who has incurred the Black
Mask's wrath - played by Ella Jay Basco.

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:49.329
Critics near-unanimously opined that this
cast, as they say, freakin' killed it.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:51.690
Courtney Howard of Fresh Fiction tweeted:

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:57.159
"Delightfully devilish &amp; deliriously wicked,
this irreverent, rule-breaking riot delivers

00:00:57.159 --> 00:00:58.399
a contact high.

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:00.940
Cathy Yan is a genius.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.239
Robbie, Smollett, Winstead, Perez &amp; Basco
are perfection."

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:10.049
Some critics disagreed amongst themselves
- not about whether or not the cast aced it,

00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:13.439
but rather around the question of who aced
it the hardest.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:18.790
Angie Han of Mashable tweeted that Winstead's
Huntress is the movie's clear MVP, while FanSided's

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:24.049
Kristen Lopez opined that Smollett-Bell's
Black Canary was, on the contrary, the movie's

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:25.250
real show-stealer.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.250
"What?"

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.509
"You are so cool."

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:32.469
Yolanda Machado of The Wrap, meanwhile, refused
to take sides.

00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:33.469
She tweeted:

00:01:33.469 --> 00:01:36.969
"It's truly an ensemble with every woman bringing
it.

00:01:36.969 --> 00:01:41.710
Christina Hodson's script was lively, funny,
&amp; everything I've been waiting for in the

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:46.899
DCEU...Cathy Yan created a Gotham that I can't
wait to revisit."

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:51.090
Chemistry among the cast is great, but Birds
of Prey is a superhero movie, and critics

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.659
also agreed that it delivers the action-packed
goods with some of the craziest, most visceral

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:57.770
fight scenes ever put to film.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.990
You heard that right: Yan and company have
apparently created a true action showcase,

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.869
the likes of which the DC films had not yet
seen.

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:09.340
Lest you think we're being hyperbolic, here's
what Rosie Knight of IGN has to say.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.340
She wrote:

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.330
"Damn [Birds of Prey] delivers!

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.190
It's a glittery hard action comedy that has
the best choreographed fight sequences I've

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.650
seen in a superhero movie.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.750
It also features my fave comic book film needle
drop ever."

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.660
Her colleague Laura Prudom agreed.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:24.660
She tweeted:

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.120
"[Birds of Prey] is a riot - oozing with attitude
and some of the most inventive, bone-crunching

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.780
fight sequences in the superhero genre to
date.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:35.570
I went in with low expectations and was pleasantly
surprised by how much fun I had.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.610
It doesn't reinvent the wheel, but has style
to spare."

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:44.050
Jill Pantozzi of io9 called the fight scenes
"phenomenal," and CinemaBlend's Sean O'Connell

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:45.730
echoed this sentiment, admitting:

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:51.590
"[Birds of Prey] is worth seeing for the kick
ass action and the Funhouse Fight Scene, alone."

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.120
The trailers for Birds of Prey gave every
indication that McGregor would give an unhinged,

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:00.510
gleefully scenery-chewing performance as Black
Mask, and we're happy to report that this

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.100
indeed appears to be the case.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:08.260
"For all your noise and bluster, you're just
a silly, little girl with no one around to

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.260
protect her."

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.820
In fact, we'd go so far as to say that early
reactions indicate that we just might be looking

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:17.970
at the best villainous performances in a DCEU
movie to date.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.390
Griffin Schiller of The Playlist tweeted:

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:26.110
"COULD NOT get enough of McGregor's Black
Mask; hysterical, eccentric, &amp; deliciously

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.110
pathetic.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.400
A rockin' kick ass good time!"

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.540
ComicBook's Brandon Davis called McGregor's
performance sinister and hilarious, while

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.120
veteran film critic Katie Walsh simply tweeted:

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.760
"FYC: Ewan McGregor, Best Supporting Actor."

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.230
McGregor did have a bit of competition, however,
from Chris Messina - who played the Black

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.680
Mask's psychopathic sidekick Victor Zsasz.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.680
Angie Han tweeted:

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.100
"Would like to send a lil prayer of thanks
for the costume, makeup, and hair people responsible

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.500
for Chris Messina's entire situation here
because wow yes thank you."

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:03.500
Of course, some reviewers jumped online to
point out some of the flick's faults.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.860
Some critics felt that the flick worked better
as a Harley Quinn solo vehicle.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.610
Others had minor issues with the pacing or
the plot.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.600
For instance, Germain Lussier of io9 tweeted:

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.350
"Birds of Prey is solid.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.960
The unpredictable structure keeps the first
half moving and the action boosts the rest.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.910
Robbie is excellent, as is McGregor.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:25.030
It's tamer than expected and the basic story
can get lost in the complex setups but it

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.780
works more often than not."

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.030
Yes, this is pretty much the closest any critic
came to a negative assessment.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:35.190
All in all, the flick was heralded as one
of DC's best - thanks in large part to Yan

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.070
and Hodson, who have apparently crafted something
pretty special.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:43.250
The DC Extended Universe may have gotten off
to a rocky start, but it looks like the franchise

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:47.710
has finally hit its stride thanks to more
universally well-received flicks like Aquaman

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:48.940
and Shazam!

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:53.370
Placing an emphasis on solid standalone movies
made by gifted, committed filmmakers has paid

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:58.970
off - go figure - and some critics went so
far as to place Birds at or near the top of

00:04:58.970 --> 00:04:59.970
the DCEU pack.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.320
Mike Rougeau of GameSpot tweeted:

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.620
"[I'm] happy to report that [Birds of Prey
is] my favorite modern DC movie yet.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.560
Like Shazam!, it carves its own path with
totally unique aesthetic, action, and tone.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.150
Margot, Ewan and all the rest are 100% fantabulous."

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.470
Mashable's Alison Foreman called the flick,
quote, "Leagues better than Suicide Squad,"

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.500
and opined that this was, quote, "in large
part because we get a rare glimpse into the

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.140
rich inner life of a female supervillain (and
it actually delivers on what was promised

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.140
in the trailer.)"

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.790
Discussing Film's Ben Rolph summed up the
consensus with his tweet.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:35.790
He wrote:

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.480
"[Birds of Prey] is a stylishly fantastic
ride.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.870
Margot Robbie is [in] top form, Harley has
never been quirkier and more lovable.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:47.650
Well-made, shot with beautiful color and overall,
a sleek piece of grand entertainment.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.770
Also, McGregor is THE BEST.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.230
We need more Birds of Prey, it's great."

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.840
Ladies and gentlemen, we have a lot to look
forward to.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.510
Birds of Prey (And the Fantabulous Emancipation
of One Harley Quinn) hits the big screen on

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.610
February 7, 2020.

